# Copy to .dev.vars (git-ignored) and fill in only what you want to enable.
# Everything is optional: with none of these set, Blueprint still generates the
# whole company, still checks domains, still plans every mailbox, and stores form
# submissions — it just records outgoing email in capture mode, leaves the
# positioning statement to the deterministic engine, and returns the Oasis
# provisioning plan without creating anything.

# --- Positioning (the one thing a model writes) ------------------------------
# Any OpenAI-compatible chat-completions endpoint. AI_BASE_URL must stop at /v1
# — the worker appends /chat/completions itself.
#
# In this estate that endpoint is the OmniRoute gateway, and the key is not
# written here: it is a `vault://` reference the dev server resolves at startup
# (see resolveVaultRefs in scripts/dev-server.mjs), so a local checkout points at
# the estate's Vault instead of holding a copy of the secret.
# AI_BASE_URL=http://192.168.1.71:20128/v1
# AI_MODEL=auto/best-chat
# AI_API_KEY=vault://cerulean/olympus#OMNIROUTE_API_KEY
# VAULT_ADDR=http://192.168.1.71:8200
# VAULT_TOKEN_FILE=.data/vault/olympus.token

# --- Oasis mail (Innotel) ----------------------------------------------------
# Oasis is the default mail provider and the only one Blueprint can provision.
# Mailboxes live on Innotel's Stalwart server; two APIs do the work:
#
#   CERULEAN_*     publishes the mail domain and its MX/SPF/DKIM/DMARC records
#                  through Cerulean's service bridge (Bearer service key, scopes
#                  `domains` and `dns`).
#   OASIS_*        creates the tenant, the mail domain and the mailboxes on
#                  Stalwart. Its configuration API is JMAP, not REST, so these
#                  are JMAP calls made with an administrative principal.
#
# Until BOTH halves are set, /api/mail/provision answers with the plan and
# creates nothing, so these are safe to leave unset.
#
# The vault:// paths below are placeholders: they only resolve once the values
# actually exist in Vault at that path. Write the tokens there first, then point
# these at them — or set the two literals directly for a throwaway local run.
# CERULEAN_API_URL=https://cerulean.innotel.us
# CERULEAN_API_TOKEN=vault://cerulean/oasis#CERULEAN_API_TOKEN
# OASIS_JMAP_URL=https://mail.innotel.us/jmap/
# OASIS_ADMIN_TOKEN=vault://cerulean/oasis#OASIS_ADMIN_TOKEN
# OASIS_JMAP_ACCOUNT_ID=
# Optional: total storage to grant the new tenant, in GB.
# OASIS_TENANT_QUOTA_GB=25

# --- Optional: outbound email ------------------------------------------------
# Blueprint's own mail (double opt-in confirmations, enquiry notifications).
# This is separate from the mailboxes it creates for a customer.
# EMAIL_PROVIDER: resend | postmark | plunk  (pair it with the matching key)
# EMAIL_PROVIDER=resend
# EMAIL_FROM="Blueprint <hello@your-domain.com>"
# RESEND_API_KEY=
# POSTMARK_SERVER_TOKEN=
# PLUNK_API_KEY=

# --- Optional: where new enquiries are announced -----------------------------
# Must be an address you control — never one supplied by a public form.
# LEAD_NOTIFY_TO=
